{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"palette","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In this mode OpenSwiftUI maps each successively defined layer in the image","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the next of the primary, secondary, and tertiary variants of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"foreground style. You can specify these styles explicitly using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/foregroundStyle(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/foregroundStyle(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifiers. If you only specify a primary foreground style, OpenSwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically derives the others from that style. For example, you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"render a filled exclamation mark triangle with yellow as the tint color","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the exclamation mark, and fill the triangle with cyan:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["Image(systemName: \"exclamationmark.triangle.fill\")","    .symbolRenderingMode(.palette)","    .foregroundStyle(Color.yellow, Color.cyan)"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also omit the symbol rendering mode, as specifying multiple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"foreground styles implies switching to palette rendering mode:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["Image(systemName: \"exclamationmark.triangle.fill\")","    .foregroundStyle(Color.yellow, Color.cyan)"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode\/palette","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A mode that renders symbols as multiple layers, with different styles","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applied to the layers.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/symbolrenderingmode\/palette"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV7paletteACvpZ","roleHeading":"Type Property","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"palette","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"palette"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/SymbolRenderingMode/palette":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode\/palette","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"palette"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","text":"SymbolRenderingMode"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A mode that renders symbols as 